  "goodToKnow": "Der Athlet is a weak noun: den Athleten, dem Athleten, des Athleten. The female form is die Athletin, and the adjective is athletisch. In everyday German, people say der Sportler or die Sportlerin for an athlete, while Athlet is typical of elite sport, such as at the Olympics (Olympische Spiele). The Greek root athlon means contest, prize. Die Leichtathletik is track and field."
